From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 04:43:14 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] test: isolate the tests that change process-wide state, and
 keep a data URL's fragment out of its HTML

Three groups failed on every run, upstream included, so the suites could not
gate a build:
- child_frame_scripts.rs: the frame-cap test set OBSCURA_MAX_LIVE_FRAMES=0
  for the whole test process, and every frame test that ran after it loaded
  no frames. It now lives in its own test binary.
- configured_font_directory_loads_nested_fonts_and_skips_symlinks: font
  directories configure a process-wide database that only the first engine
  builds, which another test had usually built already. The check now runs
  in a fresh copy of the test binary.
- css_animation_drives_autonomous_screencast_frames_until_completion: its
  data: URL wrote `#cover`, and `#` starts the URL's fragment, so the
  document ended before the animated element's rule. It is written %23.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
